  "instance_name": "developmental_disability_infantilization",
  "label": "Developmental Disability Infantilization",
  "description": "This stereotype involves portraying individuals with developmental disabilities as childlike or incapable of adult responsibilities. While not directly referenced in the image, the visual of a child’s hand being held by an adult could be misinterpreted by some as infantilizing the child, especially if the child is perceived as needing constant care. This is a real-world stereotype that can be invoked in contexts where vulnerability is emphasized.",
